            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method of optimizing control of power supply output to a resistive heating element which atomizes an aerosol source by resistance heat, comprising:a step A of measuring a resistance value of the resistive heating element;a step B of recording the resistance value measured in the step A, an adjusted power supply output determined in accordance with the resistance value as a power supply output to the resistive heating element, or identification information associated with the resistance value or the adjusted power supply output; anda step of controlling the power supply output to the resistive heating element, based on the resistance value, the adjusted power supply output or the identification information.</p>
            </abstract>
